From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:06:56 +0200
Subject: [M152] [compiler] Validate the PropertyCell value map against the
 live value

Original change's description:
> [compiler] Validate the PropertyCell value map against the live value
>
> PropertyCellData::Cache snapshots a global property cell's value, and
> the HeapObjectData constructor it reaches snapshots that value's map
> later. Between the two, StoreGlobalIC_PropertyCellCase can replace a
> kConstantType cell's value with another object of the same map, which
> leaves the cell details untouched and frees the replaced object to
> transition. Both details reads in Cache then agree while the recorded
> map describes an object the cell no longer holds.
>
> ReduceGlobalAccess feeds that map into the LoadField on the live cell,
> so optimized code could read a packed-double array's storage as tagged
> pointers. GlobalPropertyDependency checked the cell type and the
> read-only bit, StableMapDependency checked the recorded map's stability,
> and both stayed valid while describing different objects.
>
> Record the value map in GlobalPropertyDependency for kConstantType cells
> and check it against the cell's live value before installing the code.
> The map comes from the same broker snapshot the consumers read, so
> reused snapshots are covered. Maglev and Turbolev take the same
> dependency from their load and store paths, and are fixed along with
> TurboFan.
>
> Fixed: 560233248
> Change-Id: Ic992a203ae6e3973bf518cb87489d892ec0661e7
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8398508
> Commit-Queue: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
> Auto-Submit: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
